{"step_index":6941,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T13:54:19Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T13:54:19Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T13:54:23Z\nThe search for \"\"google drive\" allow upload without delete permission OR \"shared drive\" roles\" returned the following summary:\nGoogle Drive does not natively provide a way to grant \"upload-only\" access to a folder that prevents the uploader from also deleting files[1][2][3]. In both standard folders and Shared Drives, the permission levels required to add files (Editor or Contributor) inherently include the ability to delete or modify content[1][4][5].\n\n### Why this is restricted\n*   **Inherited Permissions:** In Google Drive, permissions are inherited[6][7]. If you give someone \"Editor\" access to a folder so they can add files, that same access level applies to the files within it, allowing them to delete or move them[4][3].\n*   **Shared Drive Roles:** While Shared Drives offer more granular roles than standard folders (Manager, Content Manager, Contributor, Commenter, Viewer)[8], none of these roles permit adding files without also granting the ability to edit or delete[5]. \n    *   **Contributors** can add and edit files[5].\n    *   **Content Managers** (the default for many) can add, edit, move, and delete files[8].\n\n### Recommended Workarounds\nBecause Google Drive does not support a native \"drop-box\" style permission, you can use these alternatives to achieve the same result:\n\n1.  **Google Forms (Best for file collection):** Create a Google Form and add a \"File Upload\" question type[9]. This allows users to submit files to a folder you own without them needing access to the folder itself[9][3]. They will not be able to see, edit, or delete other people's submissions[6][9].\n2.  **Third-Party Tools:** Services like *File Request Pro* or *PigeonFiles* are specifically designed to create \"upload-only\" portals for Google Drive[9][3]. These tools provide a link for users to upload files directly into your Drive without giving them any other access to your folders[10][3].\n3.  **Individual Folder Sharing (If collaboration is required):** If you are working with a small, trusted team, have them create their own folders and share them with you[6][11]. You can then move these into your master folder[11]. This keeps the files under their ownership while still centralizing them for your view[6][11].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE7-qtaR5GwBIwG4nMYmZJ_4c8jx6_mLcR1HNAAp3usaI0z7OzekV9ytRZpXGeJD8BT-zDM9h75Ukwpmp0s4h5JQvxXsP1AUkd0DxcRnEuC1-hpIkAYuUfHeIJnhAxe6vBoeKmMLIQUOK-WXzQBgzLunw1X2ILrIne3wcVC-CREFv-Bg1kwV5w2DGMyDdnprlagmBHIqfeK6CH1ej4c1Q==)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE7-qtaR5GwBIwG4nMYmZJ_4c8jx6_mLcR1HNAAp3usaI0z7OzekV9ytRZpXGeJD8BT-zDM9h75Ukwpmp0s4h5JQvxXsP1AUkd0DxcRnEuC1-hpIkAYuUfHeIJnhAxe6vBoeKmMLIQUOK-WXzQBgzLunw1X2ILrIne3wcVC-CREFv-Bg1kwV5w2DGMyDdnprlagmBHIqfeK6CH1ej4c1Q==)\n[3] [filerequestpro.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGJkEzIe3dB6mYk55Rz9vv5N50FJsrk9n9TgYBBO4ceWzOonV8rFsLqmChQ-Rfh6bZRjDb1g2Qk5cvrcMie9TXRZ89u8INfA7QAjSlTBiktdlmcdqdrqq8Lb-tLNA9jNbxDUJTRHOyOKgMYFqTNPVcmRkxqCfLLFPaoCecYCVgoJGq93QAJ4BM-nm48441O7RpZYz8=)\n[4] [nightfall.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE9nt7fEeeKXExevcc3txv6es5p5jxN96FD5dbcrPXlGpdABmc2tYdioIgy-rwT0Ib0kxdNkGkDExm66zGW2iTci-JIEq1KGsPsTFduYwX3c7YshrTPU1jSqCtigdG209Je56uW2H0Nag4-niOu)\n[5] [pipelinedigital.co.uk](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH2uLLBRjG6nZbrfdC4Ex9hHIvuBFswaVASnrKzJH85TC5uh-kxsyB79gNtIyGCtBGpv3gEJk3xJtvjmD5weFYzgcxGbPQo-ii8RoRvEfkQHFV8qQXY54yshejDst8pRyB37trWYXCflOPalh28bDMcuALVaapDkGfbkq0WEnTK1rNo9uAZlJtdF4OizK7qJN9tITrtfN0pGoJNR70=)\n[6] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE7vhSQ